repository-code: "https://github.com/m-daqdouq/Coupled-Composable-Digital-Twin-Framework-for-Off-Site-Construction"
url: "https://github.com/m-daqdouq/Coupled-Composable-Digital-Twin-Framework-for-Off-Site-Construction"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  An open-source research implementation of a Coupled-Composable Digital Twin
  (CCDT) framework for construction project management and off-site construction.
  The framework treats multiple digital twins as a system-of-systems and supports
  modeling of cross-twin physical and digital interactions, probabilistic inference,
  synchronization, and coordinated decision support. The initial reference use case
  focuses on modular/manufactured housing.
keywords:
  - digital twin
  - coupled-composable digital twin
  - off-site construction
  - modular construction
  - manufactured housing
  - construction management
  - system of systems
  - probabilistic graphical model
  - Bayesian network
  - interoperability
  - open-source ecosystem
